The Tragedy of the Commons in Ontario farming is depicted in this causal loop graphic. Large farms receive more finance, which raises production intensity, increasing short-term output and encouraging further investment (R1). However, this intensification also contributes to environmental deterioration by increasing the use of common resources like water and soil. Declining resource health eventually lowers long-term productivity, which puts pressure on producers to increase output even more (R2). The depletion of the commons is accelerated by this cycle of reinforcement. Natural constraints (B1) eventually restrict production, but only after enough harm has been done does this balancing effect take place, rendering the system less long-term viable.